        "lessons": [
          {
            "title": "Intro",
            "id": 104384,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Let's learn how to work with JavaScript <strong>template literals</strong>, which makes it easy to add variables and expressions inside of strings.</p><p>Take a look below at how template literals achieve the same result as the longer method above it.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" fullName = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Helen McGuire&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Hello &quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\" + fullName + \" /><text value=\"&quot;!&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"`Hello \" /><text value=\"${fullName}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\"!`\" /><text value=\");\" /></content><output><content><text value=\"Hello Helen McGuire!\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Hello Helen McGuire!\" /></content></output></code></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Literal string",
            "id": 104385,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Template literals make it easy to combine strings with variables through string literals.</p><p>Let's transform the string <code>\"Apple\"</code> into a string literal by enclosing <code>Apple</code> in backtick characters rather than double quotes.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" cake = \" /><text value=\"`Apple`\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(cake);\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"13\" endIndex=\"14\" /><option startIndex=\"14\" endIndex=\"19\" /><option startIndex=\"19\" endIndex=\"20\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Apple\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>`</code>, followed by <code>Apple</code>, and finally <code>`</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Template literals make it easy to combine strings with variables through string literals.</p><p>Let's transform the string <code>\"Apple\"</code> into a string literal by enclosing <code>Apple</code> in backtick characters rather than double quotes.</p><p>Store <code>Apple</code> in a template literal so the value can later include an expression.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" cake = \" /><text value=\"`Apple`\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(cake);\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"5\" /><option startIndex=\"6\" endIndex=\"10\" /><option startIndex=\"14\" endIndex=\"19\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&quot;Apple&quot;\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"'Apple'\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"Cake\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Apple\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>const</code>, followed by <code>cake</code>, and finally <code>Apple</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Variables",
            "id": 104386,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>To easily combine variables with string literals, we use the <code>${name}</code> syntax where <code>name</code> is a variable.</p><p>Code <code>${category}</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" category = \" /><text value=\"`pie`\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" cake = \" /><text value=\"`Apple \" /><text value=\"${category}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\"`\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(cake);\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"44\" endIndex=\"45\" /><option startIndex=\"45\" endIndex=\"46\" /><option startIndex=\"46\" endIndex=\"54\" /><option startIndex=\"54\" endIndex=\"55\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"(\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\")\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&amp;\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Apple pie\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>$</code> followed by <code>{</code> and then <code>category</code>, <code>}</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>To easily combine variables with string literals, we use the <code>${name}</code> syntax where <code>name</code> is a variable.</p><p>Code <code>${category}</code>.</p><p>Make the console print <code>Apple pie</code> by inserting the value of <code>category</code> after Apple.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" category = \" /><text value=\"`pie`\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" cake = \" /><text value=\"`Apple \" /><text value=\"${category}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\"`\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(cake);\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"44\" endIndex=\"45\" /><option startIndex=\"45\" endIndex=\"46\" /><option startIndex=\"46\" endIndex=\"54\" /><option startIndex=\"54\" endIndex=\"55\" /><option startIndex=\"30\" endIndex=\"34\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"$[category]\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"${category}\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"`${category}`\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Apple pie\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>cake</code>, followed by <code>$</code>, <code>{</code>, <code>category</code>, and finally <code>}</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Expressions",
            "id": 104387,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We can also perform operations inside a string literal by adding expressions inside the braces of <code>${}</code>.</p><p>Add the expression <code>quantity * price</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" quantity = \" /><text value=\"20\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" price = \" /><text value=\"10\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" cost = \" /><text value=\"`Total cost : \" /><text value=\"${quantity * price}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\"`\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(cost);\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"68\" endIndex=\"76\" /><option startIndex=\"77\" endIndex=\"78\" /><option startIndex=\"79\" endIndex=\"84\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\",\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Total cost : 200\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>quantity</code>, followed by <code>*</code>, and finally <code>price</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We can also perform operations inside a string literal by adding expressions inside the braces of <code>${}</code>.</p><p>Add the expression <code>quantity * price</code>.</p><p>Make the logged template show <code>Total cost : 200</code> by calculating the quantity times the price inside it.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" quantity = \" /><text value=\"20\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" price = \" /><text value=\"10\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" cost = \" /><text value=\"`Total cost : \" /><text value=\"${quantity * price}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\"`\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(cost);\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"66\" endIndex=\"67\" /><option startIndex=\"67\" endIndex=\"68\" /><option startIndex=\"68\" endIndex=\"76\" /><option startIndex=\"77\" endIndex=\"78\" /><option startIndex=\"84\" endIndex=\"85\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"+\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"-\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"/\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Total cost : 200\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>$</code>, followed by <code>{</code>, <code>quantity</code>, <code>*</code>, and finally <code>}</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Functions",
            "id": 104388,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>When calling a function, we leave out the parenthesis <code>()</code> if we're passing a string literal as an argument to the function.</p><p>Let's pass the string literal <code>Jane</code> while calling the <code>greetings</code> function.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" greetings = \" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"name\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") =&gt;\" /><text value=\" {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"`Bonjour \" /><text value=\"${name}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\"!`\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"};\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(greetings\" /><text value=\"`Jane`\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\");\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"82\" endIndex=\"88\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"(Jane)\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Bonjour Jane!\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>`Jane`</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>When calling a function, we leave out the parenthesis <code>()</code> if we're passing a string literal as an argument to the function.</p><p>Let's pass the string literal <code>Jane</code> while calling the <code>greetings</code> function.</p><p>Use the tagged function call that logs <code>Bonjour Jane!</code> without placing parentheses before the template literal.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" greetings = \" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"name\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") =&gt;\" /><text value=\" {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"`Bonjour \" /><text value=\"${name}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\"!`\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"};\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(greetings\" /><text value=\"`Jane`\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\");\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"73\" endIndex=\"82\" /><option startIndex=\"82\" endIndex=\"88\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"console\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"greetings(`Jane`)\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&quot;Jane&quot;\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Bonjour Jane!\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>greetings</code>, followed by <code>`Jane`</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: Literal string",
            "id": 105017,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>How do we transform a string into a string literal?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">By enclosing the string in backtick characters</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">By enclosing the string in double quotes</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">By enclosing the string in backtick characters.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>You plan to insert a variable into the text later. Which delimiters should surround the initial text now?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Backticks, to make a template literal.</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Double quotes, to make a template literal.</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">Parentheses, to make a template literal.</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Backticks, to make a template literal.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: Variables",
            "id": 105018,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What's wrong with the following code that's meant to display <code>June Jenny</code>?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" lastName = \" /><text value=\"`Jenny`\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" fullName = \" /><text value=\"`June $[lastName]`\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(fullName);\" /></content><output><content><text value=\"June $[lastName]\" /></content></output></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">We should use braces <code>{}</code> instead of square brackets <code>[]</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">We should use parenthesis <code>()</code> instead of square brackets <code>[]</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">We should use braces <code>{}</code> instead of square brackets <code>[]</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>The output contains the characters <code>$[lastName]</code> instead of Jenny. Which edit makes JavaScript evaluate the stored variable?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" lastName = \" /><text value=\"`Jenny`\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" fullName = \" /><text value=\"`June $[lastName]`\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(fullName);\" /></content><output><content><text value=\"June $[lastName]\" /></content></output></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Replace the square brackets with braces.</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Replace the square brackets with parentheses.</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">Remove the dollar sign.</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Replace the square brackets with braces.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: Expressions",
            "id": 105019,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>How do we combine expressions with string literals?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">We add expressions inside the braces of <code>${}</code> syntax</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">We add expressions after the braces of <code>${}</code> syntax</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">We add expressions inside the braces of <code>${}</code> syntax.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>In <code>`Total: ${price * quantity}`</code>, where does the multiplication belong for its result to appear in the text?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Inside the braces after <code>$</code>.</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">After the closing brace, outside the template.</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">Inside parentheses instead of braces.</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Inside the braces after <code>$</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: Functions",
            "id": 105020,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What do we leave out when calling a function with a string literal argument?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">The parenthesis <code>()</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">The backticks</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">The parenthesis <code>()</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>A template tag is followed immediately by a template literal. Which punctuation is absent before the backtick?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">The parentheses.</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">The backticks.</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">The dollar sign.</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">The parentheses.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Example: Literal string",
            "id": 105022,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Include the movie title <code>Brave</code> as a string literal.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" movie = \" /><text value=\"`Brave`\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(movie);\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"12\" endIndex=\"19\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"´Brave´\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Brave\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>`Brave`</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Store <code>Brave</code> in a constant named <code>movie</code>, using a template literal.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"movie\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"=\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"`Brave`\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".\" /><text value=\"log\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"movie\" /><text value=\")\" /><text value=\";\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"5\" /><option startIndex=\"6\" endIndex=\"11\" /><option startIndex=\"14\" endIndex=\"21\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"let\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"film\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&quot;Brave&quot;\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"'Brave'\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Brave\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>const</code>, followed by <code>movie</code>, and finally <code>`Brave`</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Example: Variables",
            "id": 105023,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Code the second string literal to combine the two into one.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" old = \" /><text value=\"`Superman`\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" latest = \" /><text value=\"`Startrek`\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" movies = \" /><text value=\"`\" /><text value=\"${old}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"${latest}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\"`\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(movies);\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" isDefault=\"true\" startIndex=\"69\" endIndex=\"78\" /></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Superman, Startrek\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>${latest}</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Example: Expressions",
            "id": 105024,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Write the code to calculate the total cost of movie tickets.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" ticketPrice = \" /><text value=\"500\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" persons = \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" total = \" /><text value=\"`Total cost: \" /><text value=\"${ticketPrice * persons}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\"`\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(total);\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"65\" endIndex=\"66\" /><option startIndex=\"66\" endIndex=\"67\" /><option startIndex=\"79\" endIndex=\"80\" /><option startIndex=\"88\" endIndex=\"89\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"(\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\")\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Total cost: 2500\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>$</code> followed by <code>{</code> and then <code>*</code>, <code>}</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>You can evaluate expressions inside a template literal by placing them between <code>${</code> and <code>}</code>.</p><p>Make the template log <code>Total cost: 2500</code> by multiplying the stored ticket price and number of people inside it.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" ticketPrice = \" /><text value=\"500\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" persons = \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" total = \" /><text value=\"`Total cost: \" /><text value=\"${ticketPrice * persons}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\"`\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(total);\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"65\" endIndex=\"66\" /><option startIndex=\"66\" endIndex=\"67\" /><option startIndex=\"67\" endIndex=\"78\" /><option startIndex=\"79\" endIndex=\"80\" /><option startIndex=\"88\" endIndex=\"89\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"+\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"-\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"/\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Total cost: 2500\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>$</code>, followed by <code>{</code>, <code>ticketPrice</code>, <code>*</code>, and finally <code>}</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Example: Functions",
            "id": 105025,
            "contentType": "interactive",
